    "---\n",
    "title: \"Multivariate Optimization: Newton, Gradient Descent, Conjugate Gradient, BFGS\"\n",
    "format:\n",
    "  html:\n",
    "    page-layout: full\n",
    "filters:\n",
    "  - shinylive\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "Set-up (once per project):\n",
    "\n",
    "``` bash\n",
    "quarto add quarto-ext/shinylive     # Quarto extension\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "``` r\n",
    "install.packages(\"shinylive\")       # R package that supplies the webR assets\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "The chunk below is self-contained: it runs in the browser through webR, so no Shiny\n",
    "server is needed and the page can be published as static HTML.\n",
    "\n",
    "**How to read the picture.** The <span style=\"color:#E8820C;\">**orange**</span> arrow is the\n",
    "steepest-descent direction $-\\nabla f(x_k)$, drawn with fixed length (direction only).\n",
    "The <span style=\"color:#2E8B57;\">**green**</span> arrow is the step actually taken,\n",
    "$\\alpha_k d_k$, from $x_k$ to $x_{k+1}$. The angle between them is what distinguishes the\n",
    "four algorithms.\n",
    "\n",
    "```{shinylive-r}\n",
    "#| standalone: true\n",
    "#| viewerHeight: 780\n",
    "\n",
    "library(shiny)\n",
    "\n",
    "## ---------------------------------------------------------------- objectives\n",
    "mk <- function(label, fv, xlim, ylim, start, xstar) {\n",
    "  force(fv)\n",
    "  list(label = label, fv = fv, f = function(p) fv(p[1], p[2]),\n",
    "       xlim = xlim, ylim = ylim, start = start, xstar = xstar)\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "FNS <- list(\n",
    "  quad = mk(\n",
    "    \"(a) Well-conditioned quadratic\",\n",
    "    function(x, y) 0.5 * (2 * (x - 1)^2 + 1.6 * (x - 1) * (y - 1) +\n",
    "                          2 * (y - 1)^2),\n",
    "    c(-3, 4), c(-3, 4), c(-2, 3), c(1, 1)\n",
    "  ),\n",
    "  ridge = mk(\n",
    "    \"(b) Narrow curved ridge (Rosenbrock)\",\n",
    "    function(x, y) (1 - x)^2 + 100 * (y - x^2)^2,\n",
    "    c(-2, 2), c(-1, 3), c(-1.2, 1), c(1, 1)\n",
    "  ),\n",
    "  mix = mk(\n",
    "    \"(c) Highly correlated, two modes\",\n",
    "    function(x, y) {\n",
    "      rho <- 0.9; den <- 1 - rho^2\n",
    "      q <- function(u, v) (u^2 - 2 * rho * u * v + v^2) / den\n",
    "      -log(exp(-0.5 * q(x - 1.2, y - 1.2)) +\n",
    "           0.6 * exp(-0.5 * q(x + 1.5, y + 1.5) / 1.5) + 1e-12)\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    c(-4, 4), c(-4, 4), c(-3, -0.5), c(1.2, 1.2)\n",
    "  )\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "## ------------------------------------------------- numerical derivatives\n",
    "num_grad <- function(f, x) {\n",
    "  h <- 1e-5 * (1 + abs(x))\n",
    "  g <- numeric(2)\n",
    "  for (i in 1:2) {\n",
    "    e <- numeric(2); e[i] <- h[i]\n",
    "    g[i] <- (f(x + e) - f(x - e)) / (2 * h[i])\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  g\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "num_hess <- function(f, x) {\n",
    "  h <- 1e-4 * (1 + abs(x))\n",
    "  H <- matrix(0, 2, 2)\n",
    "  for (i in 1:2) for (j in i:2) {\n",
    "    ei <- numeric(2); ei[i] <- h[i]\n",
    "    ej <- numeric(2); ej[j] <- h[j]\n",
    "    H[i, j] <- (f(x + ei + ej) - f(x + ei - ej) -\n",
    "                f(x - ei + ej) + f(x - ei - ej)) / (4 * h[i] * h[j])\n",
    "    H[j, i] <- H[i, j]\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  H\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "## --------------------------------------------------- Wolfe line search\n",
    "line_search <- function(f, g, x, d, a0 = 1, c1 = 1e-4, c2 = 0.9) {\n",
    "  f0 <- f(x); gd0 <- sum(g * d)\n",
    "  if (!is.finite(gd0) || gd0 >= 0) return(list(alpha = 0, ok = FALSE))\n",
    "  lo <- 0; hi <- Inf; a <- a0\n",
    "  for (it in 1:60) {\n",
    "    fa <- f(x + a * d)\n",
    "    if (!is.finite(fa) || fa > f0 + c1 * a * gd0) {\n",
    "      hi <- a; a <- 0.5 * (lo + hi)\n",
    "    } else {\n",
    "      ga <- num_grad(f, x + a * d)\n",
    "      if (sum(ga * d) < c2 * gd0) {\n",
    "        lo <- a\n",
    "        a <- if (is.finite(hi)) 0.5 * (lo + hi) else min(2 * a, 1e4)\n",
    "      } else {\n",
    "        return(list(alpha = a, ok = TRUE))\n",
    "      }\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    if (a < 1e-14) return(list(alpha = 0, ok = FALSE))\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  list(alpha = a, ok = (a > 0))\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "## ------------------------------------------------------------- algorithms\n",
    "run_alg <- function(alg, FN, x0, maxit = 60, tol = 1e-6) {\n",
    "  f <- FN$f\n",
    "  X <- matrix(NA_real_, maxit + 1, 2); G <- matrix(NA_real_, maxit + 1, 2)\n",
    "  D <- matrix(NA_real_, maxit + 1, 2); Fv <- rep(NA_real_, maxit + 1)\n",
    "  AL <- rep(NA_real_, maxit + 1)\n",
    "  x <- x0; B <- diag(2)\n",
    "  g_prev <- NULL; d_prev <- NULL; s_prev <- NULL\n",
    "  n <- 0; note <- \"maximum number of iterations reached\"\n",
    "\n",
    "  for (k in seq_len(maxit)) {\n",
    "    g <- num_grad(f, x); gn <- sqrt(sum(g^2))\n",
    "    X[k, ] <- x; G[k, ] <- g; Fv[k] <- f(x); n <- k\n",
    "    if (!is.finite(gn)) { note <- \"diverged\"; break }\n",
    "    if (gn < tol) { note <- \"converged (||grad|| < 1e-6)\"; break }\n",
    "\n",
    "    if (alg == \"nr\") {\n",
    "      H <- num_hess(f, x); H <- (H + t(H)) / 2\n",
    "      ev <- eigen(H, symmetric = TRUE, only.values = TRUE)$values\n",
    "      tau <- if (min(ev) < 1e-8) 1e-8 - min(ev) + 1e-6 * max(abs(ev)) else 0\n",
    "      d <- tryCatch(solve(H + tau * diag(2), -g), error = function(e) -g)\n",
    "    } else if (alg == \"gd\") {\n",
    "      d <- -g\n",
    "    } else if (alg == \"cg\") {\n",
    "      if (is.null(d_prev)) {\n",
    "        d <- -g\n",
    "      } else {\n",
    "        y <- g - g_prev\n",
    "        beta <- max(0, sum(g * y) / max(sum(g_prev^2), 1e-300))   # PR+\n",
    "        d <- -g + beta * d_prev\n",
    "      }\n",
    "      if (sum(g * d) > -1e-12) d <- -g                            # restart\n",
    "    } else {                                                      # BFGS\n",
    "      if (!is.null(s_prev)) {\n",
    "        y <- g - g_prev; sy <- sum(s_prev * y)\n",
    "        if (sy > 1e-10) {\n",
    "          rho <- 1 / sy\n",
    "          V <- diag(2) - rho * outer(s_prev, y)\n",
    "          B <- V %*% B %*% t(V) + rho * outer(s_prev, s_prev)\n",
    "        }\n",
    "      }\n",
    "      d <- -as.vector(B %*% g)\n",
    "      if (sum(g * d) > -1e-12) { B <- diag(2); d <- -g }\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "    ls <- line_search(f, g, x, d)\n",
    "    D[k, ] <- d; AL[k] <- ls$alpha\n",
    "    if (ls$alpha <= 0) { note <- \"line search failed (flat or non-descent)\"; break }\n",
    "\n",
    "    s_prev <- ls$alpha * d; g_prev <- g; d_prev <- d\n",
    "    x <- x + s_prev\n",
    "  }\n",
    "\n",
    "  list(X = X[1:n, , drop = FALSE], G = G[1:n, , drop = FALSE],\n",
    "       D = D[1:n, , drop = FALSE], F = Fv[1:n], A = AL[1:n],\n",
    "       n = n, note = note)\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "ALGS <- c(\"Newton-Raphson (modified Hessian)\" = \"nr\",\n",
    "          \"Gradient descent + line search\"    = \"gd\",\n",
    "          \"Conjugate gradient (PR+)\"          = \"cg\",\n",
    "          \"BFGS (quasi-Newton)\"               = \"bfgs\")\n",
    "\n",
    "## --------------------------------------------------------------------- UI\n",
    "ui <- fluidPage(\n",
    "  fluidRow(\n",
    "    column(\n",
    "      4,\n",
    "      selectInput(\"alg\", \"Algorithm\", ALGS),\n",
    "      selectInput(\"fn\", \"Objective function\",\n",
    "                  setNames(names(FNS), sapply(FNS, `[[`, \"label\"))),\n",
    "      sliderInput(\"k\", \"Iteration k\", min = 0, max = 1, value = 0, step = 1,\n",
    "                  animate = animationOptions(interval = 1000, loop = TRUE)),\n",
    "      checkboxInput(\"showpath\", \"Show the whole path\", TRUE),\n",
    "      actionButton(\"reset\", \"Reset starting point\"),\n",
    "      helpText(\"Click inside the contour plot to choose a new starting point.\"),\n",
    "      htmlOutput(\"info\")\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    column(\n",
    "      8,\n",
    "      plotOutput(\"contour\", click = \"click\", height = \"520px\"),\n",
    "      plotOutput(\"conv\", height = \"190px\")\n",
    "    )\n",
    "  )\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "## ----------------------------------------------------------------- server\n",
    "server <- function(input, output, session) {\n",
    "\n",
    "  FN <- reactive(FNS[[input$fn]])\n",
    "  start <- reactiveVal(FNS[[1]]$start)\n",
    "\n",
    "  observeEvent(input$fn, start(FNS[[input$fn]]$start))\n",
    "  observeEvent(input$reset, start(FN()$start))\n",
    "  observeEvent(input$click, {\n",
    "    p <- c(input$click$x, input$click$y)\n",
    "    if (all(is.finite(p))) start(p)\n",
    "  })\n",
    "\n",
    "  grid <- reactive({\n",
    "    FNc <- FN()\n",
    "    xs <- seq(FNc$xlim[1], FNc$xlim[2], length.out = 160)\n",
    "    ys <- seq(FNc$ylim[1], FNc$ylim[2], length.out = 160)\n",
    "    list(x = xs, y = ys, z = outer(xs, ys, FNc$fv))\n",
    "  })\n",
    "\n",
    "  path <- reactive({\n",
    "    req(start())\n",
    "    run_alg(input$alg, FN(), start())\n",
    "  })\n",
    "\n",
    "  observeEvent(path(), {\n",
    "    updateSliderInput(session, \"k\", max = max(1, path()$n - 1), value = 0)\n",
    "  })\n",
    "\n",
    "  output$contour <- renderPlot({\n",
    "    FNc <- FN(); gr <- grid(); P <- path()\n",
    "    k <- min(as.integer(input$k), P$n - 1) + 1L      # row index of x_k\n",
    "\n",
    "    zf <- gr$z[is.finite(gr$z)]\n",
    "    lv <- unique(quantile(zf, probs = seq(0, 1, length.out = 30)^1.7))\n",
    "\n",
    "    zr <- matrix(rank(gr$z, na.last = \"keep\", ties.method = \"average\"),\n",
    "                 nrow = length(gr$x))\n",
    "\n",
    "    par(mar = c(4, 4, 2.5, 1))\n",
    "    image(gr$x, gr$y, zr, asp = 1,\n",
    "          col = colorRampPalette(c(\"#f7fbff\", \"#c9dcef\"))(64),\n",
    "          xlab = expression(x[1]), ylab = expression(x[2]),\n",
    "          main = paste0(names(ALGS)[ALGS == input$alg], \"  |  \", FNc$label))\n",
    "    contour(gr$x, gr$y, gr$z, levels = lv, add = TRUE,\n",
    "            col = \"grey55\", drawlabels = FALSE)\n",
    "    points(FNc$xstar[1], FNc$xstar[2], pch = 8, col = \"red\", cex = 1.3, lwd = 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "    if (isTRUE(input$showpath) && k > 1)\n",
    "      lines(P$X[1:k, 1], P$X[1:k, 2], col = \"grey25\", lty = 2)\n",
    "    points(P$X[1:k, 1], P$X[1:k, 2], pch = 20, col = \"grey35\", cex = 0.9)\n",
    "\n",
    "    xk <- P$X[k, ]; gk <- P$G[k, ]; gn <- sqrt(sum(gk^2))\n",
    "    L <- 0.18 * diff(FNc$xlim)\n",
    "    if (gn > 0) {\n",
    "      u <- -gk / gn\n",
    "      arrows(xk[1], xk[2], xk[1] + L * u[1], xk[2] + L * u[2],\n",
    "             col = \"#E8820C\", lwd = 3, length = 0.13)\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    if (k < P$n) {\n",
    "      arrows(xk[1], xk[2], P$X[k + 1, 1], P$X[k + 1, 2],\n",
    "             col = \"#2E8B57\", lwd = 3, length = 0.13)\n",
    "      points(P$X[k + 1, 1], P$X[k + 1, 2], pch = 21, bg = \"white\",\n",
    "             col = \"#2E8B57\", cex = 1.2)\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    points(xk[1], xk[2], pch = 19, col = \"black\", cex = 1.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "    legend(\"topleft\", bty = \"n\", lwd = 3, cex = 0.95,\n",
    "           col = c(\"#E8820C\", \"#2E8B57\"),\n",
    "           legend = c(expression(-nabla * f(x[k])~\"(direction only)\"),\n",
    "                      expression(alpha[k] * d[k]~\"(step taken)\")))\n",
    "  })\n",
    "\n",
    "  output$conv <- renderPlot({\n",
    "    P <- path(); k <- min(as.integer(input$k), P$n - 1) + 1L\n",
    "    gn <- sqrt(rowSums(P$G^2))\n",
    "    gn[!is.finite(gn) | gn <= 0] <- NA\n",
    "    par(mar = c(4, 4.5, 1.5, 1))\n",
    "    plot(seq_len(P$n) - 1, gn, type = \"b\", pch = 20, log = \"y\",\n",
    "         xlab = \"iteration k\", ylab = expression(\"||\" * nabla * f * \"||\"),\n",
    "         col = \"grey40\")\n",
    "    points(k - 1, gn[k], pch = 19, col = \"#E8820C\", cex = 1.6)\n",
    "  })\n",
    "\n",
    "  output$info <- renderUI({\n",
    "    P <- path(); k <- min(as.integer(input$k), P$n - 1) + 1L\n",
    "    xk <- P$X[k, ]; gk <- P$G[k, ]; gn <- sqrt(sum(gk^2))\n",
    "    ang <- NA\n",
    "    if (k < P$n) {\n",
    "      sk <- P$X[k + 1, ] - xk\n",
    "      cs <- sum(-gk * sk) / (gn * sqrt(sum(sk^2)))\n",
    "      ang <- acos(max(-1, min(1, cs))) * 180 / pi\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    fmt <- function(v, d = 4) formatC(v, format = \"g\", digits = d)\n",
    "    HTML(paste0(\n",
    "      \"<hr><b>iteration</b> \", k - 1, \" of \", P$n - 1, \"<br>\",\n",
    "      \"<b>x<sub>k</sub></b> = (\", fmt(xk[1]), \", \", fmt(xk[2]), \")<br>\",\n",
    "      \"<b>f(x<sub>k</sub>)</b> = \", fmt(P$F[k], 6), \"<br>\",\n",
    "      \"<b>||grad||</b> = \", fmt(gn), \"<br>\",\n",
    "      \"<b>step size &alpha;<sub>k</sub></b> = \",\n",
    "      if (k < P$n) fmt(P$A[k]) else \"&ndash;\", \"<br>\",\n",
    "      \"<b>angle(orange, green)</b> = \",\n",
    "      if (is.na(ang)) \"&ndash;\" else paste0(fmt(ang, 3), \"&deg;\"),\n",
    "      \"<br><br><i>\", P$note, \"</i>\"\n",
    "    ))\n",
    "  })\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "shinyApp(ui, server)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "## Points the animation is meant to make\n",
    "\n",
    "1.  On the quadratic, Newton's step solves the model exactly: one iteration with\n",
    "    $\\alpha_k = 1$, and the two arrows differ in direction whenever the Hessian is not a\n",
    "    multiple of the identity. Conjugate gradient terminates in two iterations, BFGS in\n",
    "    roughly the same number once the inverse-Hessian approximation is built; gradient\n",
    "    descent zigzags at right angles between consecutive steps.\n",
    "2.  On the Rosenbrock ridge, the orange arrow points almost perpendicular to the valley,\n",
    "    so gradient descent makes little progress per iteration. Newton and BFGS turn the step\n",
    "    along the valley; the angle between the arrows becomes large.\n",
    "3.  On the correlated bimodal surface, the limit depends on the starting point. Clicking\n",
    "    different starting points shows convergence to different stationary points, and\n",
    "    Newton's method is attracted to whichever stationary point is nearest, including\n",
    "    saddle points when the Hessian modification is switched off."
   ]
  }
